+#### Military - Land (AI)
+
+- **Barracks**: lower `FLAVOR_MILITARY` (e.g., 10 → 6 for the generic barracks) so non-militaristic leaders don’t overbuild it; increase `iAIWeight` substantially (e.g., 0 → 70; 75 for Zulu barracks) so when built, it’s for solid ROI (earlier experienced troops). Rationale drawn partly from FFH2’s use of 40 as a baseline.
+- **Stables**: similarly increase `iAIWeight` (e.g., 0 → 75) so they’re pursued when relevant.
+- Early **siege**: adjust UnitAIs so early siege doesn’t get baited away from core attack/defense purposes.
+- New-city **minimum defenders**: ensure new cities are founded/left with **2+ defenders** (priority to capital). Optimization disabled after ~turn 120 (scaled) to save compute once empires stabilize. See **[KI#49](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#49---enhancedaddressed-ai-having-4-defenders-in-capital-city-but-only-1-defender-in-city-b-that-gets-captured-or-razed-by-barbarians-then-now-almost-always-if-not-always-new-cities-go-be-founded-with-2-defenders)**.
+- **Musketmen — AI role**: now also flagged with `UNITAI_ATTACK_CITY`, so the AI uses Musketmen more often in **offensive city-assault** roles. Civ-specific Musketman variants may also include additional changes.
+- **Grenadiers & Bazookas — AI role**: now also flagged with `UNITAI_CITY_DEFENSE`, so the AI may use them more for **city defense**.
+- **City evacuation — doomed city auto-retreat (land units only)**: in `CvUnitAI::AI_evacuateCity`, the AI now optionally (default ON, recommended) **evacuates 100% of its land units** from a **doomed city** (i.e. a city that exceeds the existing `AI_EVACUATION_THRESH`-based (default as of now: 138%) attacker/defender strength threshold (note: the threshold is raised for important cities, as it is worth defending them and generally bad to evacuate them)). Fixed an inherited Base AdvCiv percentile inversion that instead gave this important-city protection to low-value cities; see [KI#172](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#172---fixed-base-advciv-bug-inverted-city-value-percentile-gave-intended-important-city-evacuation-protection-to-low-value-cities). Previously it often retreated only a tiny fraction (e.g., 2 of 11 defenders vs a 22+ stack, whereas now all 11 defenders would evacuate if the city is deemed doomed). This change might prolong wars/game length, but the intent is a **more competitive, less self-sabotaging** AI. See [KI#62](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#62---extremely-betterstronger-ai-almost-not-evacuating-at-all-doomed-cities-2-swordsmen-in-an-11-unit-defending-stack-vs-a-22-attacking-unit-stack-fixed-by-always-and-100-evacuating-city-doomed-city-regardless-of-land-unit-type-in-cvunitaiai_evacuatecity).
+- **Minimum Stack size before war**: Added a minimum stack unit count requirement to prevent the stack from being marked as "ready" until it has enough units: no `MOVE_DECLARE_WAR` flag, no premature advance toward the city, and AI keeps building units until the stack is big enough. Helps fix the **issue of "back and forth" war declarations with immediate retreat without city attack**: low-numbered unit stacks were especially sensible to power swings (city defenses, one more enemy units skews win chance, etc.). Change in `CvUnitAI::AI_attackCityMove`. See [KI#104](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#104---tremendously-improved-base-advciv-issue-of-the-weird-back-and-forth-of-declaring-war-moving-a-stack-then-withdrawing-without-attacking-which-is-extremely-inefficient).
+- **City attack oscillation — pre-check vs strong targets (possible mitigation)**: In `CvUnitAI::AI_attackCityMove`, add a sanity check to **skip marching to/attacking a city** when the **defending stack is too strong**. Goal: prevent the inefficient **advance → abort → backtrack** loop and reduce the risk of being caught without time to retreat. **Note:** in the test sample, this behavior also resolved without the change by running ~2+ autoplay turns in a row instead of 1 turn only from a slightly older save file rather; treat this as a **possible fix/sanity check** (not (at least not yet) broadly tested). See [KI#63](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#63---possibly-prevented-and-possibly-fixed-weird--very-inefficient-back-and-forth-of-going-to-attack-a-city-stack-and-then-going-back-after-seeing-enemy-stack-is-too-strong-i-dont-know-if-this-change-fixes-it-since-the-issue-was-solved-without-it-2-autoplay-turns-were-needed-at-least-it-seems-not-1-but-maybe-this-change-in-cvunitaiai_attackcitymove-helps-a-lot-but).
+- **Early defender overbuild → switch to versatile offense (AI)**: Heuristic in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` reduces **early-game overproduction of pure defenders** (especially Longbowmen) by swapping the build to a more **offensive/versatile** unit when defense is already sufficient — e.g., Spearmen, Axemen, Camel Archers, with a preference for civ-specific units like War Chariots when available. Also caps/avoids siege (esp. Trebuchets) when they’re inefficient defensively; production can drop **down to zero** if conditions warrant. If no good replacement exists, the AI can **reflag** the chosen defender to an **attack/attack_city/counter** `UnitAI` instead. In testing, this produced **fewer pure defenders** and **more varied stacks** (e.g., a run where Hatshepsut shifted from ~30 Longbowmen at T130 to ~32 War Chariots, plus Camel Archers). See [KI#53.2](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#532---fixed-and-enhanced-joao-ai-building-way-too-many-defenders-36-longbowmen-at-turn-130-almost-all-with-unitai_city_defense-or-similar-while-being-boxed-in-with-only-3-cities-instead-of-making-about-half-of-these-offense-units-or-versatile-ones-to-punish-overextending-thin-neighbour-fixed-by-having-an-early-phase-we-have-expectedly-too-few-cities-at-this-stage-of-the-game-no-need-to-overbuild-anymore-denders-at-this-stage-of-the-game-switch-to-offense-or-versatile-unitai-rather-and-our-military-composition-has-way-too-many-defender-unitais-switch-to-offense-or-versatile-unitais-which-seemingly-fix-the-issue) and [KI#53.2.2](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#5322-seemingly-greatly-enhanced-ai-overproducing-defenders-early-on-especially-longbowmen-but-not-only-replaced-with-an-early-produce-more-versatile-units-especially-civ-specific-ones-when-defended-enough-at-least-in-theory-in-cvcityaiai_chooseunit).
+- **Siege production — conditional minimization (trebuchets especially)**: In `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit`, added targeted checks to keep **siege output** as low as needed—**up to none at all** when conditions say they’re poor value (e.g., when the AI is **weaker** or not preparing **city assaults**). Rationale: **trebuchets** are very **hammer-inefficient** outside direct city attacks; **catapults/cannons** also aren’t versatile enough (and are often misused) for defense. Current tuning intentionally leans **low** versus before (but not permanently zero when other conditions are met). Result: **more varied offensive stacks** and **stronger defense** when behind. See [KI#53.3](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#533-tremendously-improved-ai-overbuilding-siege-units-in-particular-trebuchets-but-not-only-where-they-are-detrimental-to-do-build-in-particular-when-weaker-but-not-only). **Update:** Thresholds have been **slightly relaxed pre-Renaissance**; **extra-relaxed when holding key strategic bonuses** (**Iron**, **Copper**, **Horse**, **Camel**, **Elephants**) to enable offense windows (e.g., longbow + siege); and **heavily relaxed from Renaissance onward** so **Cannons** can serve as a defensive pivot and the AI avoids over-producing Pikemen into Cuirassiers, and more generally since later sieges units are stronger and more effective, to also have a more varied and effective military composition.
+- **City-counter role pruning (e.g. Macemen)**: Removed `UNITAI_CITY_COUNTER` from **non-versatile** units (e.g., `UNIT_MACEMAN`). For example for macemen, as city defenders they’re too easy to punish—knights counter them hard, and even crossbow stacks can beat defending macemen—so they’re better assigned to **offensive** `UnitAI` roles. While macemen beat pikemen, pikes seldom assault cities efficiently, so the city-counter slot isn’t warranted. The same adjustment applies to any other units with this mismatch.
+- **Mounted "Counter" role pruning:** Removed `UNITAI_COUNTER` from the mounted units (`UNIT_CHARIOT`, `UNIT_EGYPTIAN_WAR_CHARIOT`, `UNIT_CARTHAGE_NUMIDIAN_CAVALRY`) that had it. Rationale: mounted units don’t "receive defense bonuses" (note: not related to bonuses/ressources) and can be countered by other units; assigning them to COUNTER can park them in cities (e.g. seemingly seen in autoplay with War Chariots) and occupies a slot **Longbowmen** are more fit to fill as they unlock early and are cheap and versatile defenders, so these mounted unit lines are better used for offense roles rather during its window—or skipped outside it.
+- **Stack attack order — spend expendables first:** stack attacks now prefer **bombard/collateral** and **low-effective-strength/low-XP** units first (once the stack commits to attack), preserving elite finishers. Rationale: economically efficient (older/weaker units cost upkeep but scale poorly) and strategically safer (keep high-value units for decisive blows or retreats). Change in `CvSelectionGroupAI::AI_getBestGroupAttacker`. Toggle via SAS defines for A/B testing. See [KI#89](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#89---improved-in-an-attack-stack-attack-with-lower-value-effective-strength-xp-health-units-first).
+- **Great Generals — prefer Military Instructor, focus on hammer hubs:** AI now favours settling Great Generals as **Military Instructors** over attaching them as unit leaders, as the instructor bonus scales better into the late game. **Targeting:** strong bias to the **top 3 hammer cities** with **decreasing weights** (top-1 most, then top-2/3 progressively less). Extra preference if the city **has / is building** the **Heroic Epic effect** building. **Limit removed:** cities may host **multiple** Military Instructors (no per-city cap). Implemented in `CvCityAI::AI_permanentSpecialistValue` and `CvUnitAI::AI_generalMove`. See [KI#69](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#69---tremendously-improved-ai-going-for-great-general-leaders-while-military-instructors-are-much-better-with-added-logic-to-favour-top-hammer-cities-remove-military-instructor-per-city-limit-favour-it-further-if-have-or-building-heroic-epic-effect-building-etc).
+- Update: (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6032+) Rarely in games, for example in save file 450 with France AI, a Great General could be attached to a low-value Longbowman at ~T130. BBAI logging showed the cause was Military Instructor joining was blocked by safety/path gates. To fix it, Great General unit-attachment branches now use tunable minimum target gates that default very high, so Great Generals effectively keep preferring Military Instructor or Military Academy unless these thresholds are deliberately lowered. In the retest after fix, those low-value Longbowman attachments were rejected (and another Great General attachment to USA in the same run that newly occurred as well at ~T180 was successfully blocked) and the Great Generals joined cities as Military Instructors instead. See [KI#69 (Update)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#69---tremendously-improved-ai-going-for-great-general-leaders-while-military-instructors-are-much-better-with-added-logic-to-favour-top-hammer-cities-remove-military-instructor-per-city-limit-favour-it-further-if-have-or-building-heroic-epic-effect-building-etc).
