+#### Military - Naval (AI)
+
+- Curb **naval overbuild**: in `CvCityAI::AI_bestUnit`, reduce making excess naval combat units (esp. when landlocked or when land war is likely) to prevent getting invaded on land with too few defenders. See **[KI#35](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#35---attemptingly-fixed-or-addressed-ai-building-too-many-military-naval-units-then-gets-invaded-on-land-and-cant-defend-10-galleons-and-barely-any-land-defender)**.
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6063+) **Loaded assault ships can take achievable overseas targets instead of waiting for an army larger than they can carry:** Base AdvCiv/K-Mod generally required a loaded fleet to reach a generic army size before checking whether its actual units could capture a specific city by sea. For example, BBAI logging in save file 450 showed that a fleet consisting of one Galley (total Cargo Space: 3) waited for 13 units before carrying reinforcements to an overseas attack already under way, or 26 units before launching its own full invasion. This was a problem because the fleet could not reach either threshold unless more transports joined it; more generally, any fleet whose ships together could not carry its required generic army size could remain in port indefinitely, which was especially bad when nearby Barbarian island cities sometimes even had no defenders at all. This happened even though the AI already had a more relevant check that compares its loaded units' strength with the target's defenders and route, because the generic army-size gate could prevent that check from running. To fix this, once safety, escort and imminent-loading needs are handled, a smaller loaded fleet now also asks the target-specific check whether its loaded force is strong enough to attack a reachable target. Note: the normal thresholds remain for organizing larger invasions, and the fleet still waits when no suitable target exists. For Barbarian targets, it also avoids a long naval trip to a city it expects to raze, but a worthwhile isolated-island city is not rejected merely because it is on another landmass (as per `AI_isSASCityLikelyToBenefitUsLongTerm`). In the confirming save-file 450 run, 7 distinct fleets found valid below-threshold targets, while 76 other evaluations found no acceptable target and correctly kept their fleets waiting; the changed history produced 6 additional Barbarian-city conquests with none razed. Save file 449 independently confirmed the island behavior: India sent 3 units despite a threshold of 9 and captured the Barbarian island city Burgundian six turns later. See [KI#193](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#193---fixedimproved-base-advcivk-mod-generic-army-thresholds-could-make-loaded-assault-ships-wait-instead-of-taking-achievable-overseas-targets).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6065+) **AIs can build the limited missing transport capacity needed for a nearby profitable overseas city:** the preceding fix could use a small loaded fleet, but Base AdvCiv/K-Mod could still fail to produce any assault transport for a worthwhile island. Its production logic mainly looked for a broad overseas-assault state or the complete absence of an enemy city reachable by land; therefore one unrelated land target could hide every island opportunity. A large available land army could also raise general military spending enough to block the ship needed to move it. For example, save-file 450 BBAI diagnostics found Carthage with 24 available attackers against Cimmerian's 1 defender only 9 plots from its nearest Carthaginian city, yet the missing transport was not requested. To fix this, a safe coastal city can now request only the missing cargo space when the AI knows a nearby overseas city that is worth keeping and has enough available attackers for its defenders. Existing and currently produced transports count toward that requirement, and normal financial-trouble, city-danger, defensive-war and central fleet-limit safeguards remain. In the confirming save-file 450 run, only 7 opportunistic ships were ordered, existing or queued capacity prevented 95 further requests, and all 5 tracked Barbarian targets were captured by turn 242; Cimmerian fell on turn 199 instead of turn 246 in the diagnostic run. Save file 449 independently remained restrained: 140 evaluations found that enough transport capacity already existed, only 7 opportunistic ships were ordered during 456 turns, and ordinary AI assault fleets never exceeded 4 ships. A faraway city 27 plots from the nearest Carthaginian city did not trigger new production, although Hannibal could still profitably use an existing Galleon to capture it with 4 units. See [KI#193.2](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#1932---fixedimproved-base-advcivk-mod-assault-transport-production-could-overlook-nearby-profitable-islands-when-land-armies-were-already-large-or-another-enemy-city-was-reachable-by-land).
